\caption(An exact sample covariance gives hand-checkable loadings, unique variances and the entire communality recurrence.)
\alttext(Observed variance bars contain equal common and remaining portions. A second plot shows the communalities approaching one half. Tables show all eight rows, estimated loadings, variance split and the first five iterations.)

>> Change units without changing the common fraction

Multiply all three observations by two. With standardization, the fitted correlation
is unchanged. With covariance fitting, the entire covariance is four times larger:
loadings double, and common/unique variances quadruple. The initial communalities
must therefore be 4/3, not 1/3, and the first updated value is 16/9. The final common
variance is two out of four, giving the same common fraction .5. This uniform change
of units checks the covariance-mode initialization's dimensional consistency; arbitrary
per-feature rescaling can also change eigenvalue flooring and iterative behaviour.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fa_units.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const double           a = std::sqrt(7.) / 2;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("a", std::vector<double>{a, a, 0, 0, 0, 0, -a, -a});
  d.add_column("b", std::vector<double>{a, 0, a, 0, 0, -a, 0, -a});
  d.add_column("c", std::vector<double>{a, 0, 0, a, -a, 0, 0, -a});
  for (const auto& name : std::vector<std::string>{"a", "b", "c"}) {
    auto values = d.numeric_column(name).values();
    for (auto& v : values)
      v *= 2;
    d = d.mutate(name, values);
  }
  const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis scaled(d, {"a", "b", "c"}, {1, true, "none", 1000, 1e-12});
  const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis covariance(d, {"a", "b", "c"}, {1, false, "none", 1000, 1e-12});
  const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis first(d, {"a", "b", "c"}, {1, false, "none", 1, 1e-12});
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  left.bars({1, 2, 3}, {1, 1, 1}, "observed", {148, 163, 184}, .55)
      .bars({1, 2, 3}, scaled.communalities(), "common", {37, 99, 235}, .55)
      .title("Standardized: common .5 of 1")
      .x_label("indicator (a, b, c)")
      .y_label("variance")
      .y_limits(0, 1.5);
  right.bars({1, 2, 3}, {4, 4, 4}, "observed", {148, 163, 184}, .55)
      .bars({1, 2, 3}, covariance.communalities(), "common", {37, 99, 235}, .55)
      .title("Covariance units: common 2 of 4")
      .x_label("indicator (a, b, c)")
      .y_label("variance")
      .y_limits(0, 6);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fa_units.svg");
  std::print(
      "Covariance fit:\n\n{}\n\nFirst update:\n\n{}\n\nObserved trace: {:.6f}; common share: "
      "{:.6f}.\n",
      covariance.variance_table().to_md(8),
      first.iteration_history().select({"iteration", "communality_1", "max_change"}).to_md(9),
      covariance.diagnostics().double_at("total_variance", 0),
      covariance.proportion_variance()[0]);
}
```
