\caption(A uniform factor-of-two measurement change multiplies variances by four while preserving the common fraction.)
\alttext(Standardized and covariance fits both show half of each indicator variance as common. The covariance table has observed variance four, communality two and uniqueness two. A one-step fit reports sixteen ninths as its first updated communality.)

>> Rotate a two-factor pattern and inspect the invariant fit

Start with six unit-variance indicators, with loadings .85,.80,.75 on factor A and
.70,.65,.60 on factor B, and unique variances one minus each squared loading.
For this example let B=.6*A+.8*G, where A and G are independent standard Gaussians.
The effective loadings on independent coordinates (A,G) are (.85,0),(.80,0),(.75,0),
(.42,.56),(.39,.52),(.36,.48). This is a valid correlated-generating-factor example
expressed in orthogonal coordinates, not an implemented oblique rotation.

A local seeded generator produces 500 observations. Raw and varimax models use the
same sample and extraction options. Their common covariance and per-feature common
variances must agree; the normalized varimax criterion may improve. Neither set of
individual loadings is uniquely “the true” generating factor orientation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fa_rotation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double> L(
      6, 2, {.85, 0, .80, 0, .75, 0, .42, .56, .39, .52, .36, .48});
  const auto d = dm::stats::factor_model_sample(L, {.2775, .36, .4375, .51, .5775, .64}, 500, 321);
  const std::vector<std::string>  names = {"v1", "v2", "v3", "v4", "v5", "v6"};
  const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis raw(d, names, {2, true, "none"}),
      rot(d, names, {2, true, "varimax"});
  auto left = raw.plot_loadings(), right = rot.plot_loadings();
  left.title("Unrotated loadings").x_limits(-1.6, 1.6).y_limits(-1.2, 1.25);
  right.title("Varimax: unchanged covariance").x_limits(-1.6, 1.6).y_limits(-1.2, 1.25);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fa_rotation.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame table;
  table.add_column("feature", names);
  table.add_column("raw_F1", raw.factor_loadings(0));
  table.add_column("raw_F2", raw.factor_loadings(1));
  table.add_column("varimax_F1", rot.factor_loadings(0));
  table.add_column("varimax_F2", rot.factor_loadings(1));
  std::print(
      "{}\n\nKaiser varimax objective: {:.9f} -> {:.9f}.\nCommon covariance off-diagonal "
      "difference: {:.9e}.\n",
      table.to_md(7),
      raw.diagnostics().double_at("kaiser_varimax", 0),
      rot.diagnostics().double_at("kaiser_varimax", 0),
      dm::stats::covariance_residual_rms(raw.common_covariance(), rot.common_covariance()));
}
```
