\caption(Orthogonal varimax changes the loading pattern while preserving the reproduced common covariance.)
\alttext(Two plots show the same six indicators before and after varimax. Labels identify each feature, and a unit-variance circle gives a common reference. A table and objective values distinguish changed coordinates from unchanged covariance fit.)

> Checking the theory

>> Recover common covariance across constructed samples

Return to independent generating factors, with the two three-indicator blocks above.
Their population common covariance is L*L transpose and each population feature
variance is one. We vary n=100,500,2000 and use three declared seeds at each size.
Recovery is measured against this known common covariance using off-diagonal RMS,
so signs, permutations and orthogonal rotations cannot change the answer.

For each exact same sample, also fit standardized PCA and reconstruct its covariance
from the first two eigenpairs. Compare both models against the **sample** off-diagonal
correlations. PCA optimizes a different criterion involving total variance, including
the diagonal; a smaller PAF off-diagonal residual on these generated samples is not a
general superiority claim or an optimum guarantee for PAF. Population recovery and
sample fit are separate columns. Individual replications need not improve monotonically
with n, and nine fits do not establish a sampling distribution or a confidence interval.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fa_recovery.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double> L(6, 2, {.85, 0, .80, 0, .75, 0, 0, .70, 0, .65, 0, .60});
  const auto                            target = L * L.transpose();
  const std::vector<std::string>        names  = {"v1", "v2", "v3", "v4", "v5", "v6"};
  const std::vector<double>             unique = {.2775, .36, .4375, .51, .5775, .64};
  std::vector<double> ns, seeds, recovery, fa_error, pca_error, converged, heywood;
  auto                left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors = {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}};
  std::size_t                          index  = 0;
  for (unsigned seed : {123, 321, 777}) {
    std::vector<double> grid, errors;
    for (std::size_t n : {100, 500, 2000}) {
      const auto                       d = dm::stats::factor_model_sample(L, unique, n, seed);
      const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis  fit(d, names, {2, true, "varimax", 1000, 1e-8});
      const dm::stats::PCA             pca(d, names);
      std::vector<std::vector<double>> columns;
      for (std::size_t c = 0; c < 2; ++c) {
        auto v = pca.loadings().col(c);
        for (auto& x : v)
          x *= std::sqrt(pca.explained_variance()[c]);
        columns.push_back(v);
      }
      const auto   P = dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>::from_columns(columns);
      const double r = dm::stats::covariance_residual_rms(target, fit.common_covariance());
      const double f = fit.diagnostics().double_at("offdiagonal_rms", 0);
      const double e =
          dm::stats::covariance_residual_rms(pca.covariance_matrix(), P * P.transpose());
      ns.push_back(n);
      seeds.push_back(seed);
      recovery.push_back(r);
      fa_error.push_back(f);
      pca_error.push_back(e);
      converged.push_back(fit.converged() ? 1 : 0);
      heywood.push_back(fit.diagnostics().double_at("heywood_variables", 0));
      grid.push_back(std::log10(n));
      errors.push_back(r);
    }
    left.line(grid, errors, "seed " + std::to_string(seed), colors[index])
        .points(grid, errors, "", colors[index], 4);
    ++index;
  }
  left.title("Recovery of known common covariance")
      .x_label("log10 sample count")
      .y_label("off-diagonal RMS")
      .y_limits(0, .12);
  right.points(fa_error, pca_error, "same samples", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .line({0, .14}, {0, .14}, "equal residual", {148, 163, 184})
      .title("Sample residuals solve different tasks")
      .x_label("PAF off-diagonal RMS")
      .y_label("PCA off-diagonal RMS")
      .x_limits(0, .15)
      .y_limits(0, .2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fa_recovery.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame table;
  table.add_column("n", ns);
  table.add_column("seed", seeds);
  table.add_column("population_common_RMS", recovery);
  table.add_column("PAF_sample_RMS", fa_error);
  table.add_column("PCA_sample_RMS", pca_error);
  table.add_column("converged", converged);
  table.add_column("Heywood", heywood);
  std::print("{}\n", table.to_md(7));
}
```
