| 2000 | 123 | 0.0158787 | 0.0060141 | 0.1000678 | 1 | 0 |
| 100 | 321 | 0.0520771 | 0.0268993 | 0.1118930 | 1 | 0 |
| 500 | 321 | 0.0440913 | 0.0130158 | 0.1004483 | 1 | 0 |
| 2000 | 321 | 0.0230020 | 0.0038874 | 0.1007050 | 1 | 0 |
| 100 | 777 | 0.0692954 | 0.0122644 | 0.1044803 | 1 | 0 |
| 500 | 777 | 0.0376980 | 0.0090833 | 0.0966754 | 1 | 0 |
| 2000 | 777 | 0.0184706 | 0.0035293 | 0.0995004 | 1 | 0 |

\image(figures/fa_recovery.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Repeated known-model samples distinguish recovery of population common covariance from residual fit to each sample.)
\alttext(Three lines show common-covariance recovery errors for three seeds and three sample sizes. A second plot compares PAF and PCA sample off-diagonal residuals on identical data, with an equality line. A table includes stopping and Heywood flags for every fit.)

Across these seeds, population common-covariance RMS falls from .0521–.0693 at n=100
to .0159–.0230 at n=2000. All nine fits stop without a Heywood violation. PAF sample
residuals are .0035–.0269, while rank-two PCA residuals are .0937–.1119 on these same
samples. Those numbers describe this specified generating model and these replications.

> Iris: inspect a strained factor model

`dm::datasets::iris()` contains 150 rows, four numeric measurements in centimetres and
species labels. Use all four numeric columns, standardize them, and keep species out
of fitting. The first rows make the schema explicit. Iris is a familiar counterexample
for fit diagnostics, rather than evidence that species are generated by these factors.

For p=4, k=1 has parameter-count df=2, while k=2 has df=−1. Fit both with the same
stopping controls and show what the implementation actually does. Report convergence,
raw uniqueness and observed-versus-reproduced off-diagonal correlations together.
A positive df does not prevent an improper fit, and a smaller covariance residual does
not rescue an overparameterized or nonconverged one. Inspecting diagonal mismatch is
necessary because the compatibility uniqueness output is clamped.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fa_iris.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto                     d     = dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::vector<std::string> names = {
      "Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"};
  const dm::stats::FactorAnalysis one(d, names, {1, true, "none"}),
      two(d, names, {2, true, "varimax"});
  const auto v1 = one.variance_table(), v2 = two.variance_table();
  auto       left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  left.bars(
          {.83, 1.83, 2.83, 3.83},
          v1.numeric_column("raw_uniqueness").values(),
          "one factor",
          {37, 99, 235},
          .3)
      .bars(
          {1.17, 2.17, 3.17, 4.17},
          v2.numeric_column("raw_uniqueness").values(),
          "two factors",
          {220, 38, 38},
          .3)
      .line({.5, 4.5}, {0, 0}, "boundary", {148, 163, 184})
      .title("Raw uniqueness reveals the violation")
      .x_label("SL=1, SW=2, PL=3, PW=4")
      .y_label("observed minus common variance")
      .y_limits(-.2, 1.35);
  const auto          a = one.covariance_pairs(), b = two.covariance_pairs();
  std::vector<double> observed, fitted1, fitted2;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.nrows(); ++i) {
    if (a.string_at("feature_i", i) == a.string_at("feature_j", i))
      continue;
    observed.push_back(a.double_at("observed", i));
    fitted1.push_back(a.double_at("reproduced", i));
    fitted2.push_back(b.double_at("reproduced", i));
  }
  right.points(observed, fitted1, "one factor", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .points(observed, fitted2, "two factors", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .line({-.6, 1.05}, {-.6, 1.05}, "exact fit", {148, 163, 184})
      .title("Off-diagonal agreement is only one check")
      .x_label("observed correlation")
      .y_label("reproduced correlation")
      .x_limits(-.6, 1.05)
      .y_limits(-.6, 1.65);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fa_iris.svg");
  const auto columns = std::vector<std::string>{
      "factors",
      "iterations",
      "converged",
      "degrees_freedom",
      "heywood_variables",
      "offdiagonal_rms",
      "max_diagonal_excess"};
  std::print(
      "Iris: {} rows, {} numeric model features.\n\n{}\n\nOne factor:\n\n{}\n\nTwo "
      "factors:\n\n{}\n\nOne-factor variance split:\n\n{}\n\nOne-factor loadings:\n\n{}\n",
      d.nrows(),
      names.size(),
      d.head(3).to_md(2),
      one.diagnostics().select(columns).to_md(7),
      two.diagnostics().select(columns).to_md(7),
      v1.to_md(7),
      one.loading_table().to_md(7));
}
```
